# SemText npl-mood — affective-state chip, all display modes
# Direction A "Slate Console" (house convention). Three example panels in one
# frame, one per display mode the tag provides: the enhanced full form (chip +
# generated detail panel), the enhanced chip-only form (self-closing), and the
# JS-off degraded form (no chrome). The invariant the design must broadcast:
# npl-mood is display-only and QUIET — a small rounded badge that shows the
# mood at a glance, never an opaque accent block, and it never occludes or
# hides the authored text (occlusion belongs to the sem-spoiler / quiz tier).
#
# MODE 1 — enhanced, full form (chip + detail panel):
#   visible: a compact rounded-pill badge at the left — a small emoji-scale
#     glyph slot, then the qualifier as small-caps accent-tinted text; below
#     it, a grouped detail panel of up to three small-caps labelled lines
#     (tone · / context · / approach ·), each label muted and dimmer than its
#     value.
#   must never: fill the chip opaque; render the qualifier as part of the
#     value sentences; hide or drop the detail lines; put the chip after the
#     panel.
# MODE 2 — enhanced, chip-only (self-closing / lone emoji):
#   visible: the same rounded badge, glyph plus (optional) small-caps
#     qualifier, alone — no detail panel, no leading label line.
#   must never: invent a panel, a label, or extra chrome the tag does not
#     define; restyle the chip differently from mode 1.
# MODE 3 — JS-off degraded:
#   visible: the mood as a plain lead line (glyph + qualifier, normal
#     weight, foreground colour) followed by the authored tone / context /
#     approach children as ordinary unstyled prose lines — no badge, no
#     labels, no border.
#   must never: show a pill/badge, generated small-caps labels, or any chrome
#     when the script has not run; hide any authored line.
#
# The emoji is the mood's glyph — it is the one place a real character may
# appear; everywhere else the mock uses abstract placeholder bars, never
# letters, digits, or words.
#
# Reference renders: the site's /reference/npl-mood/ page is source-view only
# today, so the enhanced form is judged from a throwaway fixture captured with
# the room's headless Chrome (fixture HTML + current themes/_vocabulary.css +
# the built npl.js). The `npl-mood-render-*` references below are those
# fixture captures; `npl-mood-fullpage-1280.png` is the site page (source view
# + page chrome) from `npm run snap:tag -- npl-mood`.
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-npl-mood
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of three side-by-side reference-page panels
    illustrating one affective-state chip element in its three display
    modes, wide 16:9, flat technical illustration (screenshot-like, not
    3D). Dark slate navy background (#0F172A) with a barely visible thin
    grid and a faint violet radial glow upper-left. Three equal panels sit
    side by side, separated by thin slate hairline dividers, each panel a
    dark slate card (#1E293B) with a thin slate hairline border, squared
    corners, deep soft shadow; a small dim caption bar sits above each
    panel.

    LEFT panel — ENHANCED FULL FORM. At the panel's top-left sits a small
    rounded-pill badge (fully rounded ends, hairline slate border, a barely
    there lighter slate fill over the card, NOT solid colour): inside it a
    single soft-violet rounded glyph square holding one abstract spark
    shape (never a real emoji), followed by one short small-caps scale
    placeholder bar in a light violet tint — the qualifier. Below the badge,
    indented slightly, sit three stacked lines, each led by a short, muted,
    dimmer small-caps placeholder label bar followed by a wider brighter
    near-white value bar of differing length; the labels are clearly dimmer
    than their values.

    MIDDLE panel — ENHANCED CHIP-ONLY. The identical rounded-pill badge
    alone, glyph square plus the single small-caps qualifier bar, centred in
    generous empty card space; no lines beneath it, no labels, no border
    change — pixel-comparable to the left panel's badge.

    RIGHT panel — JS-OFF DEGRADED. No badge and no chrome: the mood reads
    as one plain foreground-coloured lead line at the panel's top-left — a
    glyph square (a neutral, un-tinted outline square holding the abstract
    spark) followed by a normal-weight near-white placeholder bar of the
    qualifier's length — and beneath it two or three plain prose lines of
    near-white placeholder bars with NO small-caps labels, NO pill, NO
    tint, NO border. It must read as unstyled authored prose.

    Across all three panels the mood glyph square stays small and quiet; the
    chips/badges are tinted, never filled opaque, and no line of text in any
    panel is occluded, blurred, or dimmed below its label.
  negative: legible text, letters, numbers, digits, words, captions,
    typography, watermark, logo, light mode, white cards, 3D, photorealism,
    faces, avatars, robot mascots, more than three panels, an opaque filled
    badge, a solid colour-block chip, a badge in the right panel, small-caps
    labels in the right panel, real emoji characters, a detail panel in the
    middle panel, a qualifier bar fused with its value sentences
  style: flat dark-mode product UI illustration, squared corners, hairline
    borders, slate and violet palette, three-panel mode comparison

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-mood/npl-mood-render-enhanced-900.png
    role: reference
    description: enhanced render — chip + detail panel, chip-only, lone emoji, data-mood spelling (fixture)
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-mood/npl-mood-render-jsoff-900.png
    role: reference
    description: JS-off render — mood as a plain lead line, authored children as prose (fixture)
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-mood/npl-mood-fullpage-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: site reference page (source view) — chrome, attribute table, example placement

requirements:
  subject: three panels of one affective-state chip — left enhanced full form
    with a rounded badge and a three-line detail panel, middle enhanced
    chip-only badge, right JS-off plain lead line plus prose
  palette: slate navy background, slate panels, hairline borders, violet
    accent on the qualifier and glyph, near-white value bars, muted labels
  composition: three equal panels side by side, each badge/lead line at a
    consistent top-left position, identical chip anatomy across the two
    enhanced panels
  do:
    - keep the chip a small tinted rounded-pill badge, never an opaque block
    - keep every value bar brighter than its muted small-caps label
    - differentiate modes only by panel presence and chrome presence
  dont:
    - any legible text, digits, real emoji (but the single mood glyph), or logos
    - occluding, blurring, or dimming any line in any panel
    - a badge, border, or generated label in the right (JS-off) panel
    - extra chrome (badges, counts, buttons) the tag does not define

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  required_pass:
    - mode_differentiation
    - quiet_not_opaque
  criteria:
    mode_differentiation:
      weight: 3
      description: Left panel shows the badge plus a three-line labelled detail
        panel; middle shows the badge alone; right shows a plain lead line and
        unstyled prose with no badge or label
      fail_signals:
        - badge or pill present in the right panel
        - detail panel present in the middle panel
        - small-caps labels in the right panel
        - chip anatomy differs between the two enhanced panels
    quiet_not_opaque:
      weight: 3
      description: The chip is a small tinted rounded-pill badge, never a solid
        opaque colour block, and no text is occluded, blurred, or dimmed below
        its label in any panel
      fail_signals:
        - opaque or solid accent-filled chip
        - value bars dimmer than their labels
        - blur, redaction, or occlusion overlays on any bar
    theme_fidelity:
      weight: 2
      description: Dark slate + violet, squared hairline panels, flat style
      fail_signals:
        - light theme
        - glossy 3D look
        - rounded card corners
  reject_if:
    - any legible text, letters, digits, real emoji beyond the mood glyph,
      watermark, or logo
    - an occluded, blurred, or hidden line in any panel
    - a badge, border, or generated label in the JS-off panel
    - more than three panels or a chaotic layout

tags:
  - semtext
  - reference
  - npl-mood